# Ollama Modelfile for the pentest agent's structured-output model.
#
# RECOMMENDED MODEL: BaronLLM (AlicanKiraz0/Cybersecurity-BaronLLM_Offensive_Security_LLM_Q6_K_GGUF)
# -- an offensive-security fine-tune of Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct. Chosen over
# the other commonly-found "kali-pentester" Llama-3.1 GGUF fine-tunes after
# empirical A/B testing through this agent's real Ollama /api/chat + JSON
# schema pipeline (not just a guess):
#   - BaronLLM's GGUF has a properly embedded tokenizer.chat_template (the
#     stock Meta Llama-3.1-Instruct template) and the correct instruct EOS
#     token (<|eot_id|>, 128009) -- confirmed via `gguf_dump.py --no-tensors`
#     against the file. That means NO custom TEMPLATE directive is needed
#     below; Ollama uses the model's own embedded template automatically.
#   - Other "kali-pentester" Llama-3.1 fine-tunes found in the wild (e.g.
#     suryanshp1/Llama-3.1-8B-kali-pentester) are fine-tuned from the raw
#     *base* checkpoint with no chat_template embedded and a base EOS token
#     (128001) -- meaning they need a hand-built Alpaca-style TEMPLATE (see
#     Modelfile.alt-base-completion in this directory) and, in side-by-side
#     testing, followed this agent's structured tool-call parameter-naming
#     instructions far less reliably (frequently emitted generic param1/
#     param2/param3 keys instead of the real target/service/wordlist keys
#     tools.py expects) than BaronLLM did across every test prompt.
#
# This is a checked-in template, not something runnable from this repo as-is
# -- the FROM path below must point at a GGUF file that actually exists on
# the Ollama HOST (a separate machine from this orchestrator), and the model
# is built and registered there, not here:
#
#   scp baronllm-llama3.1-v1-q6_k.gguf ollama-host:/path/to/models/
#   # on the Ollama host, after adjusting FROM below:
#   ollama create pentest-agent -f Modelfile
#
# Then set OLLAMA_MODEL=pentest-agent (matching the name you gave `ollama
# create`) and OLLAMA_HOST=http://<that host>:11434 in this orchestrator's
# .env. See docs/SETUP.md for the full walkthrough.

FROM /path/to/models/baronllm-llama3.1-v1-q6_k.gguf

# Keep this in sync with OLLAMA_NUM_CTX in .env -- it's used there only for a
# prompt-size warning heuristic, but the real ceiling is set here.
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096

# Low temperature / top_p: this model's only job is picking a tool chain
# from a fixed, schema-constrained vocabulary, not creative generation.
# (BaronLLM's own model card recommends temperature 0.3 for "deterministic
# reasoning tasks" -- 0.1 tested at least as reliably for pure tool-call
# selection and is more conservative; raise toward 0.3 if you want more
# varied tool choices.)
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_p 0.9

# No TEMPLATE directive -- BaronLLM's GGUF already embeds the correct chat
# template. Do not add one unless you switch to a model without an embedded
# tokenizer.chat_template (check first: `ollama show <model> --modelfile`).

SYSTEM """You are an autonomous penetration testing agent. You will be given \
a goal and must respond with a JSON tool chain matching the schema you are \
given. Do not include any prose, explanation, or markdown -- only the \
structured JSON response."""
